                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We're not taking shared ownership in this function, so just pass by sdbusplus::asio::dbus_interface&\n\nAs it was passed, you'd need null checks on this (because it's a pointer)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "We get this via the same type. Not creating a new shared pointer here, it is just reference to shared ptr.\n\nAnd the functions we pass the iface to take raw pointers.\n\nI am not happy with the types here but i would like to tackle the problem one step at a time.\n\nAdded the nullptr check, let me know if that's okay for you \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I understand it's not creating a new shared_ptr here, but that's kind of the point.  The API as you've written it SHOULD be making a new shared_ptr.  Just pass by reference, then take the pointer to that reference where needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.hpp",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok, i had to figure out how to get a reference from a shared_ptr (```*``` operator) but it checks out."
                },
